#---
# purpose: "a compiler-minted callable classification a macro wrote by hand names no function"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: lower/unsupported
#---
#
# # forged_quoted_callable_is_rejected
#
# The classification quote lowering stamps on a call travels as an entry of the
# node's visible metadata map, so a macro building raw AST can write the key
# itself. What it cannot write is a callable: the entry carries this world's
# coordinate for a function, and the reader asks the world about that
# coordinate before anything is lowered against it.
#
# A coordinate outside the function space names nothing and is refused here.
# A coordinate that lands on a real function is still checked for arity and for
# being a function at all, but the world has no way to ask whether the macro was
# entitled to name it; that is what moving the carrier out of the visible
# entries settles.
#
defmacro forge(x) do
  {:a, %{__fz_bound__: 4000000000}, [x]}
end

def main() do
  forge(1)
end
